# add_two — user operation + value-returning call + integer output.
# Exercises: user-op invocation, `out VALUE` binding (bind value), a second
# operation, and console.writeIntegerLine. (todos WS1-040, WS1-050/051, WS1-105)

AddTwo is project
AddTwo module examplesAddTwo
AddTwo target console
AddTwo entry main

examplesAddTwo is module
examplesAddTwo path examples.addTwo
examplesAddTwo exports main
examplesAddTwo purpose "Add two integers and print the sum"
examplesAddTwo invariant "main is the only project entry operation"

addTwoValues is operation
addTwoValues in leftValue Int64
addTwoValues in rightValue Int64
addTwoValues out Int64
addTwoValues memory heap no
addTwoValues async no
addTwoValues purpose "Return the sum of two signed 64-bit integers"
addTwoValues invariant "Performs no effects; pure arithmetic"
addTwoValues do sumCall
addTwoValues return sumValue

sumCall is call
sumCall in addTwoValues
sumCall invokes math.addInt64
sumCall arg left Int64 leftValue
sumCall arg right Int64 rightValue
sumCall out sumValue Int64

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Compute 40 + 2 and write the result"
main invariant "Writes exactly one integer line"
main let leftInput immutable Int64 40
main let rightInput immutable Int64 2
main let successExitCode immutable ExitCode 0
main do answerCall
main do writeAnswer
main return successExitCode

answerCall is call
answerCall in main
answerCall invokes addTwoValues
answerCall arg leftValue Int64 leftInput
answerCall arg rightValue Int64 rightInput
answerCall out answerValue Int64

writeAnswer is call
writeAnswer in main
writeAnswer invokes console.writeIntegerLine
writeAnswer arg value Int64 answerValue

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32
ExitCode purpose "Process exit status"

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout
stdoutWriter purpose "Allow controlled writes to standard output"
